Description: Don't drop hotplugged outputs when the primary KMS device has no renderer
 On split display/render SoCs (Apple Silicon: "apple" KMS device + separate
 "asahi" render-only GPU) no EGL device matches the KMS fd, so initMgpu()
 always fails. Startup tolerates this (backend not ready yet), but after a
 hotplug SDRMConnector::connect() bailed out and the monitor never appeared.
 The primary backend doesn't need the mgpu renderer (it only gathers GL
 formats), so treat the failure as non-fatal and stop retrying on every commit.
Author: Omarchy Debian port
Forwarded: no
--- a/src/backend/drm/DRM.cpp	2026-11-20 12:31:50.512638560 +0100
+++ b/src/backend/drm/DRM.cpp	2026-11-20 12:31:50.524440733 +0100
@@ -641,7 +641,16 @@
         if (rendererState.renderer && rendererState.allocator)
             return true;
 
-        return initMgpu();
+        // primary device without a usable renderer (e.g. Apple display controller):
+        // not fatal, and don't retry on every commit.
+        static std::unordered_set<const void*> noRenderer;
+        if (noRenderer.contains(this))
+            return true;
+        if (!initMgpu()) {
+            backend->log(AQ_LOG_ERROR, std::format("drm: no renderer for primary {}, continuing without it", gpu->path));
+            noRenderer.insert(this);
+        }
+        return true;
     }
 
     const bool hasEnabledOutputs =
